### 24.3 Number Theoretic Functions

#### 24.3.1 The Mobius Function

I. Definitions

\[\begin{array}{l}\text{I.}\ \mu(n)=1\\ \text{if }n=1\\ \text{=}(-1)^{n}\text{if }n\text{ is the product of }k\text{ distinct primes}\\ =0\text{if }n\text{ is divisible by a square }>1.\end{array}\]

B. Generating functions

\[\begin{array}{l}\sum\limits_{n=1}^{n}\mu(n)n^{-r}=1/\zeta(s)\\ \sum\limits_{n=1}^{n}\frac{\mu(n)\,\overline{x}^{n}}{1-x^{n}}=x\\ \text{II.}\ \text{Relations}\end{array}\]

A. Recurrence

\[\begin{array}{l}\mu(mn)=\mu(m)\mu(n)\text{ if }(m,n)=1\\ =0\text{ if }(m,n)>1\end{array}\]

B. Check

\[\begin{array}{l}\sum\limits_{d\text{in}}\mu(d)=\delta_{n1}\end{array}\]

